{%- comment -%}
  A moved page. MLn now lives in its own repo (mlnclub/mlnclub.github.io) and
  serves from its own domain, but the /mln/ and /mln/week-N/ URLs have been
  shared publicly for months — in every Luma event description, in chat, on a
  QR code — so each one stays put here and forwards.

  Deliberately not the site's normal chrome: this page is a signpost, not a
  destination, and pulling head.liquid would drag the whole stylesheet chain in
  for markup nobody looks at. `robots: noindex` plus a canonical pointing at
  the new URL is what moves the search ranking across instead of leaving two
  competing copies of every week.

  To use: give a page `layout: redirect` and a `redirect_to`.
{%- endcomment -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ site.lang }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>Redirecting to {{ page.redirect_to }}</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ page.redirect_to }}">
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ page.redirect_to }}">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <style>
      body { font: 16px/1.5 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
             margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: flex; align-items: center;
             justify-content: center; text-align: center; padding: 1.5rem;
             background: #1f3329; color: #ece1c8; }
      a { color: #d8c4a0; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>The MLn Reading Club has moved to <a href="{{ page.redirect_to }}">{{ page.redirect_to }}</a>.</p>
    <script>window.location.replace({{ page.redirect_to | jsonify }});</script>
  </body>
</html>
